  "kind": "quirk",
  "title": "SEC computes RN53(RN64(1 / COS(x))) over the x87 COS chain and rejects |x| >= 2^27 with #NUM!",
  "statement": "In Excel 16.0.20131 through 16.0.20527, SEC(number) applies the circular-trig domain limit (|x| >= 2^27 returns #NUM!) and evaluates RN53(RN64(1 / COS(x))) using Excel's raw x87 COS chain (which inherits FLDPI/2 range reduction at large arguments and returns 1.0 for |x| < 2^-26). Under compat-1, @SEC returns #NAME?. All 2,138 full-bank SEC rows match.",
  "status": "measured",
  "basis": "Measured across Excel 16.0.20131, 20430, and 20527.20088, matching 2,138/2,138 full-bank and 120/120 pinned SEC rows.",
